# Gimnasio Fuego (C7, contract 53), 17 x 24, interior. The forge: BIG light stone slabs (`slab_<i%2><j%2>`, never small tiles), the two back walls, braziers (animated flames) in the dead ends of the lanes and beside the leader, and
# the QUIZ MACHINES: the hall is cut by SIX walls (j = 19, 16, 13, 10, 7, 4), each with one door (a key-door actor that vanishes with its flag, `gate=yes`) at the right (i = 13) or the left (i = 3) end alternately, so the
# way is a serpentine of lanes. Beside every door a machine (OK) asks a yes / no question in the four languages: the right answer opens the door at once; a wrong one makes the lane's toll trainer fight (a win opens it too, a loss is the
# blackout). PROFESOR BRASA (script NPC, the camera cuts to him) waits at the top (8,2): a win = the Medalla Brasa (flag 86, `badge_brasa`, the card's 7th badge) + Disc 10 (flag 861).
@map gimnasio_fuego
@size 17 24
@interior yes
@bg 0
@fill slab_11
@flag quiz_d1 862        # the door of quiz machine 1 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag quiz_d2 863        # the door of quiz machine 2 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag quiz_d3 864        # the door of quiz machine 3 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag quiz_d4 865        # the door of quiz machine 4 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag quiz_d5 866        # the door of quiz machine 5 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag quiz_d6 867        # the door of quiz machine 6 is open (the answer was right, or the toll trainer lost)
@flag brasa_disc 861       # Profesor Brasa handed over the Fire disc (a full bag keeps it clear)
@spawn door 8 22 N
@legend
  .  tile=none object=gym_wall_j
  a  tile=slab_11
  b  tile=slab_10
  c  tile=slab_01
  d  tile=slab_00
  e  tile=air_0
  f  tile=none object=gym_wall_i
  g  tile=slab_10 object=brazier
